{
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "blocker",
      "claim": "The spec's citations into saffron/cell/session.py and saffron/cli.py, used as literal build instructions and not just background, point to the wrong code at this base because the spec was read at an earlier commit (bc879e2c) and session.py/cli.py changed hundreds of lines in between. _rebut_gates is cited at :3091-3108 but is actually at :3346-3363. _judge is cited at :2590-2594 but is actually at :2810. The ORPHANED-on-exception logic is cited at :3304-3310 but that range writes wrong-versions.json, with the real logic near :3563-3565. probe_findings is cited at :1506-1663 but is actually at :1717, and _probe_adequacy is cited at :2966-2979 but is actually at :1877. Step 7's two unproven-reason prefixes are cited at :1618-1627 with a second use at :1787, but the real prefixes sit at :1830 and :1837 inside probe_findings, :1787 holds an unrelated comment, and the only other literal occurrence of the first prefix is at :1998 inside the out-of-scope _apply_criterion_probes function, so step 7's second instruction cannot be satisfied as written. Step 4's cap-path rewrite of result.why is cited at :3171-3179 but the real rewrite is at :3432. The finishing suite's reverify call is cited at saffron/cli.py:783-791 but is actually at :843-850. The CellOutcome test stand-ins are cited at tests/test_package.py:773-791 (actually :871) and tests/test_session.py:10998 (actually :11607). A cell that resolves these by line number rather than re-deriving them from the named identifiers would edit the wrong code, and step 7 cannot be satisfied literally at all since its only real second match lives in explicitly out-of-scope code.",
      "criterion": null,
      "file": "saffron/cell/session.py",
      "line": null,
      "fixes": "build"
    },
    {
      "severity": "concern",
      "claim": "The spec's caveat that every line number was read at bc879e2c gives no indication of which files drifted or by how much, so a reader cannot tell without independently diffing the two commits that saffron/cell/session.py and saffron/cli.py, the two files criteria 2, 3, 5, 6 and the PACKAGE criterion most depend on, moved hundreds of lines between bc879e2c and the stated base, while saffron/gates/core/revert.py, saffron/gates/suite.py, saffron/probe.py, saffron/phases/review.py and saffron/phases/rebut.py, cited just as heavily, did not move at all. An operator should decide whether to let a cell discover and route around this drift on its own turns and budget, or refresh the citations before launch.",
      "criterion": null,
      "file": null,
      "line": null,
      "fixes": null
    }
  ]
